1
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Roller Coaster Rabbit is a family, comedy,
animation film directed by Rob Minkoff.

2
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Roger Rabbit struggles to keep wandering Baby Herman safe in an
amusement park where the usual havoc ensues.

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Roger Rabbit (voice), played by Charles Fleischer.

4
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Jessica Rabbit (voice), played by Kathleen Turner.

5
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Young Baby Herman / Mrs. Herman (voice), played by April Winchell.

6
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Adult Baby Herman (voice), played by Lou Hirsch.

7
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Droopy Dog (voice), played by Corey Burton.

8
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Bull (voice), played by Frank Welker.

9
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
The Roger Rabbit shorts are a series of three live-action/animated short films
produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation from 1989 to 1993.

10
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:26,000
They feature Roger Rabbit, the animated protagonist from Who Framed Roger Rabbit (1988), being enlisted to care for
Baby Herman while his mother is absent, resulting in a plot defined by slapstick humor and visual gags.

11
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Each short concludes with a sequence involving live-action and animation, in which the
characters interact with live-action human beings, akin to the 1988 film.

12
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Droopy Dog from MGM makes a cameo in all of the shorts.

13
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Charles Fleischer, Kathleen Turner, Lou Hirsch, and April Winchell returned to reprise their voice roles from
the film, alongside producers Steven Spielberg, Kathleen Kennedy, Frank Marshall, and Don Hahn.

14
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Marshall also directed the live-action segments in the first two shorts, while Industrial
Light & Magic (ILM) was responsible for the live-action visual effects.

15
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Produced in association with Spielberg's Amblin Entertainment, the three shorts (Tummy Trouble, Roller Coaster Rabbit
and Trail Mix-Up) were originally attached to the theatrical releases of several Disney and Amblin films.

16
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:26,000
A fourth short, Hare in My Soup, was cancelled during pre-production, with three more (Clean and
Oppressed, Beach Blanket Bay and Bronco Bustin' Bunny) in the planning stages also cancelled.

17
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Despite being produced by Walt Disney Animation, these shorts heavily
contained a similar slapstick style to Warner Bros.

18
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Looney Tunes or Tex Avery cartoons, and MGM
character Droopy made cameos in every one.

19
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:26,000
The film explores themes of cartoon, roller coaster
/ rollercoaster, cartoon rabbit.

20
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:46,000
The tone is lighthearted.
